[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
MDWeb has been installed.

1. Create a JWT secret file (mode 0600, owned by www). Do not put the
   secret in rc.conf or on the command line:

     umask 077
     openssl rand -hex 32 > /usr/local/etc/mdweb/jwt.secret
     chown www:www /usr/local/etc/mdweb/jwt.secret
     chmod 0600 /usr/local/etc/mdweb/jwt.secret

   The rc script sets JWT_SECRET_FILE to that path. Any other mode
   refuses to start.

2. Copy sample config if needed:

     cp /usr/local/etc/mdweb/config.json.sample \
       /usr/local/etc/mdweb/config.json
     cp /usr/local/etc/mdweb/users.json.sample \
       /usr/local/etc/mdweb/users.json
     chown www:www /usr/local/etc/mdweb/config.json \
       /usr/local/etc/mdweb/users.json
     chmod 0600 /usr/local/etc/mdweb/users.json

   service.host defaults to 127.0.0.1. security.corsOrigins is an
   allowlist (never "*"). Rate limits on /api/login, /api, and /mcp
   return HTTP 429 when exceeded.

3. Create the admin. There is no admin/admin password. The password
   comes from stdin or a mode-0600 file, never argv:

     cd /usr/local/www/mdweb
     env CONFIG_DIR=/usr/local/etc/mdweb \
       ./node_modules/.bin/tsx server/scripts/bootstrap-admin.ts --issue-token
     printf '%s\n' 'a-long-password' | env CONFIG_DIR=/usr/local/etc/mdweb \
       ./node_modules/.bin/tsx server/scripts/bootstrap-admin.ts \
       --username admin --setup-token 'THE_TOKEN'

   Later password changes:

     printf '%s\n' 'a-new-password' | env CONFIG_DIR=/usr/local/etc/mdweb \
       ./node_modules/.bin/tsx server/scripts/change-password.ts admin

4. Enable and start:

     sysrc mdweb_enable=YES
     service mdweb start

Health check: curl http://127.0.0.1:5173/api/health
Audit log: /usr/local/etc/mdweb/audit.log (JSON lines; no tokens or passwords)
EOM
}
